{"nodes": [{"id": "raw_engineering_debt_2026_08_02_table", "label": "Engineering Debt Register (2026-08-02)", "file_type": "image", "source_file": "raw/engineering-debt-2026-08-02.png", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": "2026-08-02", "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "raw_engineering_debt_2026_08_02_ed_1", "label": "ED-1 (MED): Gate 5 (deflate bounded-memory) under-powered", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "raw/engineering-debt-2026-08-02.png", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": "2026-08-02", "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Gate 5's deflate body fits one pako batch. Interest: the K5 relay-balloon risk (fast feed + slow listener growing bodyStream) is untested; a real regression would pass CI. Principal: add a large-deflate paced-feed case. Named in the final review."}, {"id": "raw_engineering_debt_2026_08_02_ed_2", "label": "ED-2 (MED): 3 upstream tests depend on network/cache fixtures", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "raw/engineering-debt-2026-08-02.png", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": "2026-08-02", "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The 99.8% pass rate, not 100%. Interest: red suite noise on every clean machine; reviewers learn to ignore failures \u2014 the worst habit a gate can teach. Principal: vendor the fixtures hermetically or mark and quarantine the suites."}, {"id": "raw_engineering_debt_2026_08_02_ed_3", "label": "ED-3 (LOW): Truncation parity edges \u2014 divergent error contracts", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "raw/engineering-debt-2026-08-02.png", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": "2026-08-02", "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Stream throws Error; buffered throws {exception, dataSet}; mid-FMI truncation emits partial events before throwing. Interest: error-handling code written against one path mishandles the other. Principal: unify the error contract; document